+# ADR 074: Restricted `_CoqProject` mappings for Rocq
+
+## Status
+
+Accepted for the ProofBridge managed-artifact integration.
+
+## Threat addressed
+
+The verifier previously compiled only a flat `Module.v` under the synthetic
+`-Q . TBCI` namespace. A valid Rocq project whose target identity depends on
+repository mappings could therefore not be reconstructed independently. The
+verifier must derive that identity without executing producer-controlled build
+logic.
+
+## Decision
+
+The Rocq adapter may read a root `_CoqProject` containing only complete
+`-Q <directory> <logical>` and `-R <directory> <logical>` triples. Paths must
+remain inside the verifier-owned clean workspace and logical names must be
+valid Rocq module names. The target source basename must be unique. The
+adapter derives the qualified module and compiles the target's local import
+closure serially in dependency order before checking the target.
+
+Unknown `_CoqProject` tokens, ambiguity, cycles, path escape, oversized files,
+or malformed local dependency declarations fail closed. When `_CoqProject` is
+absent, the existing flat `-Q . TBCI` behavior remains unchanged.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Executing `Makefile`, `dune`, shell flags, or arbitrary project commands.
+- Claiming support for every Rocq build-system feature or generated source.
+- Expanding the trusted result beyond the frozen task contract and observed
+  source-only workspace.
+- Changing the Lean or Isabelle adapters.
+
+## TCB impact
+
+The trusted computing base gains only the bounded mapping/import parser and
+the verifier-owned dependency-order planner. Producer build scripts remain
+outside the TCB because they are never executed.
+
+## Verdict semantics
+
+An accepted mapping changes how the contracted module is located and checked;
+it does not relax target, environment, kernel, trust, snapshot, or delta
+evidence. Unsupported or ambiguous project state is an error and cannot yield
+`Trusted`.
+
+## Exit checks
+
+- Flat Rocq regression remains green.
+- A namespaced `_CoqProject` fixture with a local imported theorem verifies.
+- Unsupported options, ambiguous target basenames, and dependency cycles fail.
+- Portable Lean and Isabelle adapter regressions remain green.
